        66["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Item Matcher</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: SciPy linear_sum_assignment]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Matches predicted to gold<br />items per row by optimal<br />assignment on category and<br />amount tolerance; the<br />matching rule is part of the<br />metric definition version.</div>"]
        style 66 fill:#f4f4f6,stroke:#aaaaac,color:#272834
        67["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Error Taxonomy Classifier</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: Python]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Labels each mismatch: bad<br />classification, wrong count<br />(over / under), not enough<br />categories, wrong amount, low<br />confidence, irreproducible.</div>"]
        style 67 fill:#f4f4f6,stroke:#aaaaac,color:#272834
        68["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Metric Engine</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Component: pandas, scikit-learn]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Computes accuracy, coverage<br />($ and rows), AUC, cost of<br />inference, evidence<br />verifiability, approval rate,<br />reproducibility and<br />calibration from the metric<br />definition registry; adds<br />per-carrier views and the<br />Level 3 cost-driver summary.</div>"]
        style 68 fill:#f4f4f6,stroke:#aaaaac,color:#272834
